{"slug":"persian","name":"Persian","blurb":"Persian has been written in three scripts: the cuneiform of the Achaemenid kings, scripts drawn from Aramaic for Middle Persian, and since the 9th century the Arabic alphabet with four letters of its own.","scripts":[{"id":"perso","label":"Persian alphabet","engine":"letters","rules":"persian","font":"system","dir":"rtl","material":"parchment","vowelmarks":"1","about":"New Persian in the Arabic script, with پ چ ژ گ added for sounds Arabic lacks; the alphabet of Ferdowsi, Rumi and Hafez, and of Persian today.","note":"Type as it sounds: sh, ch, zh, kh, gh for ش چ ژ خ غ. Long ā becomes ا, i and u become ی and و; short a, e and o inside a word are not written, and a final e is the silent ه (nāme). The letters that Persian took from Arabic are on the keys, with the sound they have in Persian.","groups":[["Letters",[["ā","ا","alef · a long a, or the seat of a first vowel"],["b","ب","be · b"],["p","پ","pe · p"],["t","ت","te · t"],["s̱","ث","se · s (in Arabic words)"],["j","ج","jim · j"],["č","چ","che · ch"],["ḥ","ح","he · h (in Arabic words)"],["x","خ","khe · ch as in loch"],["d","د","dāl · d"],["ẕ","ذ","zāl · z (in Arabic words)"],["r","ر","re · r"],["z","ز","ze · z"],["ž","ژ","zhe · s as in pleasure"],["s","س","sin · s"],["š","ش","shin · sh"],["ṣ","ص","sād · s (in Arabic words)"],["ż","ض","zād · z (in Arabic words)"],["ṭ","ط","tā · t (in Arabic words)"],["ẓ","ظ","zā · z (in Arabic words)"],["ʿ","ع","eyn · a catch in the throat"],["ġ","غ","gheyn · a gargled g"],["f","ف","fe · f"],["q","ق","qāf · a gargled g"],["k","ک","kāf · k"],["g","گ","gāf · g"],["l","ل","lām · l"],["m","م","mim · m"],["n","ن","nun · n"],["w","و","vāv · v; also u and o"],["h","ه","he · h; also a final e"],["y","ی","ye · y; also i"]]],["Hamza and joining",[["ʾā","آ","alef madda · a first ā"],["ʾ","ء","hamze · a catch in the throat"],["|","‌","half-space · keeps two parts apart (mi|ravam)",3]]],["Numbers and punctuation",[["0","۰","0",3],["1","۱","1",3],["2","